    {
      "page_title": "Task Status, Restarts & Deletes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Status trap",
          "items": [
            "Connector RUNNING, tasks FAILED — normal",
            "Always read task state, not connector state",
            "Restarting a connector skips failed tasks",
            "Unless `includeTasks=true`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Restart And Remove"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "GET /connectors/pg-src/status",
            "POST /connectors/pg-src/restart",
            "  ?includeTasks=true",
            "DELETE /connectors/pg-src"
          ],
          "note": "read the task trace first"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Worker restarts keep configs — they live in `config.storage.topic`",
            "`DELETE` drops the config; ==source offsets== stay behind",
            "Recreate under the **same** name → resumes from those offsets"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Source Connectors: JDBC vs Log CDC",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Worker config is process-level: `bootstrap.servers`, `plugin.path`, converters",
            "Connector config is per-connector and overrides converters"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Parallelism costs connections",
          "text": "More tasks = more parallelism and more open sockets. A JDBC source at 50 tasks can drain the database connection pool."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Job Of A Source",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Discover work units (tables, files, shards)",
            "Poll for new data on an interval",
            "Emit `SourceRecord`: key, value, schemas, source offset"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "JDBC Query Modes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Reads",
            "Blind to"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`bulk`",
              "all rows each poll",
              "nothing, but brutal"
            ],
            [
              "`incrementing`",
              "new IDs only",
              "updates, deletes"
            ],
            [
              "`timestamp`",
              "newer `updated_at`",
              "late commits"
            ],
            [
              "`timestamp+incrementing`",
              "both columns",
              "deletes"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Clock-skew problem: a row commits with an older timestamp than one already read",
            "`timestamp.delay.interval.ms` buys the in-flight transactions time",
            "`timestamp+incrementing` is the safest query mode"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Log-Based CDC"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "JDBC (query)",
                "lines": [
                  "no special privileges",
                  "polls the table",
                  "misses deletes",
                  "adds DB load"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Debezium (log)",
                "lines": [
                  "reads binlog/WAL/LogMiner",
                  "insert+update+delete",
                  "before/after images",
                  "needs replication rights"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "{\"before\":{...}, \"after\":{...},",
            " \"source\":{...}, \"ts_ms\":1725,",
            " \"op\":\"u\"}   # c create u update",
            "             # d delete r snapshot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Config Skeleton"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "connector.class=...MySqlConnector",
            "tasks.max=1",
            "database.hostname=db.prod",
            "topic.prefix=shop",
            "table.include.list=shop.orders  # + converters"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ValueToKey` copies `id` from value into a Struct key",
            "`ExtractField$Key` unwraps it to the bare ==id==",
            "Compaction and sink upserts now key on the PK"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Tombstones, Snapshots & Keying By PK",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Delete emits the change event plus a null-value record on the same key",
            "That tombstone is what lets log compaction erase the entity",
            "`snapshot.mode=initial|never|schema_only|when_needed`",
            "Snapshot first, then switch to streaming"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Topics And Keys"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Topic is usually `<prefix><table>`; `topic.prefix` is mandatory in modern Debezium",
            "Key on the primary key so compaction and upserts work",
            "Null key = round-robin = per-entity ordering destroyed",
            "Ordering is per-partition only, never global"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Snapshot Modes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`initial`",
              "snapshot, then stream"
            ],
            [
              "`never`",
              "stream only"
            ],
            [
              "`schema_only`",
              "schema, no rows"
            ],
            [
              "`when_needed`",
              "snapshot if offsets lost"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Keying By PK"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "transforms=vk,x",
            "transforms.vk.type=...ValueToKey",
            "transforms.vk.fields=id",
            "transforms.x.field=id"
          ],
          "note": "x is ExtractField$Key: Struct → id"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Clock-Skew Guard"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "mode=timestamp+incrementing",
            "timestamp.column.name=updated_at",
            "incrementing.column.name=id",
            "timestamp.delay.interval.ms=5000"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "One binlog, one task",
          "text": "Debezium MySQL reads a single binlog, so it runs **one** task whatever `tasks.max` says. Scale by splitting databases, not tasks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Sink Connectors: Upserts, Batches & Lag",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Postgres slots",
          "items": [
            "A slot holds WAL until it is consumed",
            "Stopped connector = primary disk fills",
            "Alarm on `pg_replication_slots`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Renaming is not free",
          "text": "Connect keys source offsets by connector name. Rename the connector and the offsets vanish — you get a full re-snapshot of the table."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shape Of A Sink",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reads a `topics` list or a `topics.regex`, writes to an external store",
            "At-least-once by default — the target must tolerate duplicates",
            "Idempotency comes from upserting on a key, not from Kafka"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "JDBC Sink Keys"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Setting",
            "Values",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`insert.mode`",
              "insert / upsert / update",
              "`upsert` for idempotence"
            ],
            [
              "`pk.mode`",
              "`none`, `kafka`",
              "`kafka` = topic/part/offset"
            ],
            [
              "`pk.mode`",
              "`record_key`",
              "the standard pick"
            ],
            [
              "`pk.mode`",
              "`record_value`",
              "field from the payload"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`auto.create=true` builds the table from the record schema",
            "`auto.evolve=true` issues `ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN`",
            "Evolve only ADDs nullable columns — never drop, rename, narrow",
            "Anything else is a planned migration"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Files And Batches"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Sink",
            "Knob",
            "Risk"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "JDBC",
              "`batch.size`",
              "poll interval blown"
            ],
            [
              "any",
              "`consumer.max.poll.records`",
              "rebalance storm"
            ],
            [
              "S3",
              "`flush.size`",
              "small-files problem"
            ],
            [
              "S3",
              "`rotate.interval.ms`",
              "latency vs file size"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sinks are consumer groups — the ==LAG== column is the truth",
            "Alarm on `sink-record-lag-max` per task",
            "Oversized batches blow `max.poll.interval.ms` → rebalance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Tombstones in sinks",
          "items": [
            "JDBC: `delete.enabled=true` needs `pk.mode=record_key`",
            "Elasticsearch: `behavior.on.null.values=delete`",
            "Otherwise nulls are skipped or fail the task"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "S3 & Elasticsearch Sinks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "S3 partitioners: `DefaultPartitioner`, `FieldPartitioner`, `TimeBasedPartitioner`",
            "Time-based needs `path.format`, `partition.duration.ms`, `timezone`",
            "Elasticsearch: `write.method=upsert`, doc ID from the record key",
            "`behavior.on.null.values=ignore|delete|fail` decides tombstone handling"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Watching Sink Lag"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kafka-consumer-groups \\",
            "  --bootstrap-server kb:9092 \\",
            "  --describe \\",
            "  --group connect-pg-sink"
          ],
          "note": "status API never shows lag"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Error Handling & Converters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Error Handling"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "errors.tolerance=all",
            "errors.deadletterqueue.topic.name=dlq-x",
            "errors.deadletterqueue.context.headers.enable=true",
            "errors.retry.timeout=60000  # bounded retry",
            "errors.retry.delay.max.ms=5000"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`errors.tolerance=none` is the default: one poison record kills the task",
            "Correct, but the pipeline stops at 3am — choose deliberately",
            "Retries run before anything reaches the DLQ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Consumer Overrides"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "consumer.override.auto.offset.reset=earliest",
            "consumer.override.max.poll.records=200",
            "# worker must allow it:",
            "connector.client.config.override.policy=All"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Delete ≠ replay",
          "text": "Recreating a sink connector under the same name reuses consumer group `connect-<name>` and its committed offsets. It resumes where it stopped; it does not reprocess the topic."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Bytes Happen",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Converter translates Connect `SchemaAndValue` ⇄ raw wire bytes",
            "Source = serialize, sink = deserialize — same class, both directions",
            "`key.converter` and `value.converter` are set independently",
            "Common pairing: `StringConverter` key, Avro value"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Connect's Data Model"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Schema` carries type, name, optional, default, version",
            "`Struct` holds the record fields against that schema",
            "Logical types: `Decimal`, `Date`, `Time`, `Timestamp`",
            "Logical = an annotated primitive with a logical name"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "// schemas.enable=true, every message:",
            "{\"schema\":{...},\"payload\":{...}}",
            "// schemas.enable=false:",
            "{\"id\":7}   # sinks get a bare Map"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Embedded schema is self-describing and hugely bloated",
            "Schemaless JSON makes the JDBC sink refuse the record",
            "Neither gives you central governance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Converters are topic-wide",
          "text": "The converter is a contract on the topic, not a setting on your connector. Every producer and every consumer must agree, Connect included."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Wire Formats & Schema Registry",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Converters"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Converter",
            "Wire",
            "Schema"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`StringConverter`",
              "UTF-8",
              "none, lossy"
            ],
            [
              "`ByteArrayConverter`",
              "pass-through",
              "none, opaque"
            ],
            [
              "`JsonConverter`",
              "JSON",
              "embedded or off"
            ],
            [
              "`AvroConverter`",
              "binary + ID",
              "registry"
            ],
            [
              "`Protobuf`/`JsonSchema`",
              "binary/JSON + ID",
              "registry"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Registry Wire Format"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "0x00",
              "ID b3",
              "ID b2",
              "ID b1",
              "ID b0",
              "payload…"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [],
            "highlight": [],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "5 bytes of overhead per record"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "value.converter.schema.registry.url=http://sr:8081",
            "value.converter.schemas.enable=false",
            "value.converter.enhanced.avro.schema.support=true",
            "# worker sets defaults, connector overrides"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Picking A Format"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Format",
            "Size",
            "Governance"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "JSON + schema",
              "3-5× larger",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "Avro",
              "compact",
              "registry, evolvable"
            ],
            [
              "Protobuf",
              "compact",
              "polyglot codegen"
            ],
            [
              "JSON Schema",
              "readable",
              "governed middle"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "`Unknown magic byte!`",
          "items": [
            "An Avro converter read a non-Avro record",
            "Usually plain JSON, or a String key",
            "Check `key.converter` first — it is the usual culprit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What It Actually Is",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A REST service storing versioned schemas, handing out globally unique int IDs",
            "Its storage is one compacted topic, `_schemas`",
            "The service is stateless — it rebuilds from that log on restart"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Subjects"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A subject is the namespaced scope that versions and compatibility checks hang off. Strategy picks the name."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Subject Strategies & Registry Ops",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Strategy",
            "Subject",
            "Fits"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`TopicNameStrategy`",
              "`<topic>-value`",
              "one type per topic"
            ],
            [
              "`RecordNameStrategy`",
              "`com.x.OrderCreated`",
              "type across topics"
            ],
            [
              "`TopicRecordNameStrategy`",
              "`<topic>-<record>`",
              "event union, one topic"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Both Paths"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "local cache miss",
              "POST register",
              "get ID",
              "prepend 5 bytes",
              "consumer fetch by ID",
              "decode"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Registry REST Calls"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Verb",
            "Path",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "GET",
              "`/subjects`",
              "list subjects"
            ],
            [
              "GET",
              "`/subjects/{s}/versions`",
              "version history"
            ],
            [
              "GET",
              "`/schemas/ids/{id}`",
              "fetch by ID"
            ],
            [
              "POST",
              "`/subjects/{s}/versions`",
              "register"
            ],
            [
              "PUT",
              "`/config/{s}`",
              "set compat mode"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Dry-Run In CI"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "POST /compatibility/subjects/",
            "  orders-value/versions/latest",
            "{\"schema\":\"...\"}",
            "→ {\"is_compatible\":true}"
          ],
          "note": "checks without registering anything"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Prod producers",
          "items": [
            "`auto.register.schemas=false`",
            "`use.latest.version=true`",
            "Register from CI, **never** from a deploy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Soft `DELETE /subjects/{s}` only hides the subject",
            "`?permanent=true` frees versions — can strand consumers",
            "Registry down: cached IDs work, ==new IDs stall=="
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
